{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>I am weary of my life because of the daughters of Heth.</b> You will find the ק of קצתי is small (זעירי) in the Masorah, and the reason for this is that Rivka saw through ru'aḥ ha-kodesh that the House and the Temple were destined to be destroyed — which was a hundred cubits — on account of the sin of Israel intermarrying with the daughters of the land. And corresponding to it, we find in the book of Tehillim a large ק (רבתי) — that is, as it is written (Psalms 84): ״גם צפור מצאה בית ודרור קן לה״ — because King David prepared silver and gold in abundance for the building of the Temple, and he would pray concerning the building of the House and the Temple that it should be a hundred cubits, for he already knew this measurement through ru'aḥ ha-kodesh along with all the other measurements of all the vessels; as it says (I Chronicles 28:19): ״הכל בכתב מיד ה׳ עלי השכיל כל מלאכת התבנית״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:43.409458536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}